Subject: The generator can read the property names of an object-literal template

What this does
  - `JSAotGenFunc` gains `objlit_count`, `objlit_atoms[i]` and `objlit_nprops[i]`: the property names of object-literal template i, in the order `object_fill` stores its window. The names are copied (from the template, or from its shape once the template has been used), so the generator owns them.
  - `js_aot_gen_free` releases them.

Why we need it
  The bundle analysis follows which value an object literal puts under which name (the property descriptor `{value: f}` of `Object.defineProperty(Object.prototype, "inheritsFrom", ...)`, a configuration object, a literal with fields). The register program only carries the template index.

Soundness
  Generator-side data only; no unit code and no runtime path reads it.

Functions touched
  `js_aot_gen_collect`, `js_aot_gen_free`, `JSAotGenFunc`.

No.

